   "text": "The pattern fits a single phase, Dy2MnNiO6 (mp-1104659). The fit holds only if its cell is about 1.5% smaller than the CIF cell, which is an assumption.\n\n**Observed peaks.** Main peaks (2\u03b8, relative intensity) are 23.6\u201324.0 (about 17), 26.5 (30), 32.5 (30), 33.85 (100), 34.65 (36), 43.6 (14), 48.3 (12), 49.75 (16) and 54.4 (17).\n\n**Dy2MnNiO6.** Removing the cell skew gives a near-orthogonal perovskite cell with a \u2248 5.59, b \u2248 5.26 and c \u2248 7.55 \u00c5.\n- From this cell, the characteristic perovskite peaks fall at:\n  - (200) about 32.0\u00b0\n  - (112) about 33.3\u00b0\n  - (020) about 34.0\u00b0\n  - (110)/(002) about 23.2\u201323.6\u00b0\n  - (111) about 26.05\u00b0\n  - (113) about 43.0\u00b0\n- Shrinking the cell by about 1.5% moves these to 32.5, 33.85, 34.6, 23.6\u201323.9, 26.45 and 43.6\u00b0.\n- That matches the observed peaks closely, including the triplet with the strongest peak in the middle.\n\n**Other candidates.** Each is missing a strong reflection the pattern would need, or puts its strongest peak in the wrong place.\n- **TaTiGaO6:** a trirutile should have its strongest peak, (110), near 26.9\u00b0, which does not fit.\n- **Yb2Al2O5:** it predicts peaks at about 27.2\u00b0 and 34.5\u201334.8\u00b0 but cannot produce the 32.5\u201334.65\u00b0 triplet.\n- **Zr5Sn3O:** its main peaks fall near 32.2\u00b0 and 35.8\u00b0, which do not match.\n- **KEuO2:** it should have (003) at about 14\u00b0 and (012) at about 30.3\u00b0; neither is present.\n- **Ca3GeO, SrPrMgRuO6, LiVCrO4 and Li4MnCr3O8:** their peak positions are clearly offset from the observed ones.\n\nI see no peaks that need a second phase.\n\n{\"present\": [\"mp-1104659\"], \"confidence\": 0.8, \"note\": \"Orthorhombic-perovskite peak set (110/002 ~23.8, 111 ~26.5, 200/112/020 triplet at 32.5/33.85/34.65 deg) matches Dy2MnNiO6 with an assumed ~1.5% smaller cell; no other candidate fits and no second phase is needed.\"}",
